Z||000003||falconhulk||12-06-2001||08:31 AM||||Heh I would rather have a crank then power windows.  Replacing a motor sucks.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||12-06-2001||11:35 AM||||That's what I thought 14 years ago when I bought my car new. But luckily I ordered my car with them they have worked perfectly all those years. I don't hear too often about these going bad in Fieros. I guess that's one thing GM did good.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000005||falconhulk||12-06-2001||12:23 PM||||Mine also work Alex but I had to replace in my Firebird!  What a pain drilling out rivits and messing with that regulator.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fie Ro||12-06-2001||01:06 PM||||I got the windowmotors out of my crashed GT and it was a pain to get (grind!) them out  of the demolished doors so I think to get them in will be quite a sh*tty job also. The mounting points were quite difficult to reach what I can recall...<P>power mirrors should be a lot easier to do.||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||12-06-2001||01:32 PM||||The only way I've done this is to swap both entire doors... if you're going to be doing a repaint, do the swap. If not repainting, swapping the doors and then swapping the doorskins back might be easier than mucking with the insides of the doors to access all the mounting points, etc.... <P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show 2001||||reg||1
Z||000008||cadaver||12-07-2001||12:32 AM||||I put power windows, locks and mirrors. And a few other things in my 86SE. You can swap the doors and then swap the skins back if you want. Personally its more of a pain then to just swap in the parts you need. Did mine in a afternoon.||||reg||1
Z||000009||BUCK WILLIAMS||12-08-2001||12:06 AM||||THANKS FOR YOU HELP!  I LOOKED AT OGRE'S SITE AND FOUND INFO. WHOLE DOOR SWAP MIGHT BE THE EASIEST WAY TO GO.  I AM GONNA PAINT THE CAR ANYWAY AND NEED TO REPLACE THE DOOR SKIN ON DRIVER'S SIDE ANYWAY. ENJOY YOUR FIEROS AND THANKS AGAIN!!!||||reg||6
Z||000010||theogre||12-08-2001||12:38 AM||||I swapped the hole door and put my OE skin back on it... Keep in mind tho... I've been messing with car doors for around 25 years. There are ticks to the door/window system. I've tried to describe them all in my cave but it's as much an art as science. <P>Total time, including a decent try of refinishing a set of mirrors was probably around 40 hours. <P>If you want power mirrors, check Monkeyman's project in my cave. That's the only way to go if you don't have the whole OE kit, including good door skins....<P>Some people will tell you that you can't move the doors from one year to another. I don't buy it. Maybe it's true for 84 but even then I doubt it...<P>It's complicated to explain.<P>The reason, I think, people say the doors can't move is that most people simply don't understand that there are a group of inter related adjustments involved..... Getting them righ is a b_tch even when you know how.<P>first you've got to adjust the door right. not as easy as it seems. Only the door side of the hinge is adjustable but it's really crabby about being just so.<P>Then you've got half a dozen window adjustments. mess up these and the window or the seal can be damaged really fast. I have ssen people break glass getting it wrong.<P>on top of that there are adjustments to the door skin. That one is not in my cave yet...<P>the door skin is referenced to only ONE screw.<P>all the other screws are installed. THEN the skin is tweeked to clear the front and rear edges properly.<P>Once that is set, then the last screw is shot.<P>This is the screw near the lock. It's a self drilling screw shot into the plastic plug by the lock after the skin position is set.<P>That one screw is what makes allot of people think the mill/drill process fits the doors to an individual car.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||cadaver||12-08-2001||01:57 AM||||That is why I find it easier to just swap the motors into the  original doors.||||reg||1
